    "text": "Electrophile attack where the electron density high.which shows +M or +I effects are ortho/para directing because they increase electron density at ortho and para +M&nbsp; &nbsp;<math><mo>-</mo><mover><mrow><mtext>N</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo>•</mo><mtext> </mtext><mo>•</mo></mrow></mover><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mo>-</mo><mover><mrow><mtext>N</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo>•</mo><mtext> </mtext><mo>•</mo></mrow></mover><mo>=</mo><mtext>O</mtext><mo>,</mo></math> <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/db2a5b5c-6149-4815-90e3-6f454858219e.png\" style=\"width:0.98792in;height:0.4649in\" />, <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/04cbbb60-08bb-433a-a900-0de695221e9c.png\" style=\"width:1in;height:0.41772in\" />, <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/rqwetrgsdfas.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 33px;\" /><br />The following groups are meta directing <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/65f275be-4b3f-47a9-b974-938dff73d9b8.png\" style=\"width:0.57297in;height:0.45755in\" /> ,<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/78606ebd-234d-459b-be82-45afba3611eb.png\" style=\"width:0.58977in;height:0.43844in\" />, <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> They decreases electron density at ortho/para so, electrophile attack at meta position.",
